course: dictionary
lesson: 8200
title: Resurrection: coming back to life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A resurrection is the act of coming back to life. The word has a clue inside it: re- means again, and rise means to get up. For Christians the most important example is Jesus, and «the Resurrection of Jesus» means his rising from the dead.
explain: Context helps you here. «Christians believe the Resurrection is the heart of their faith; Easter Sunday celebrates it.» The words faith and celebrates show that this is a serious religious belief. Look for more clues too: «the empty tomb is its sign».
explain: The word also works outside religion. «The resurrection of an old toy craze» means something forgotten that has come back into use. So ask what the sentence is about, a religious idea or something that returned, and choose the meaning that fits.
fact: Resurrection is a noun. Its plural is resurrections.
fact: «The Resurrection» with a capital R means the rising of Jesus from the dead on the third day after his crucifixion.
fact: Christians celebrate the Resurrection at Easter.
fact: In everyday English, «resurrection» can mean something old brought back into use.
fact: Christians, Ukrainians and others have different beliefs about death, but many people try to answer the same question about life and memory.
exercise: In «the Resurrection of Jesus», what does Resurrection mean? | A famous old church building | A birthday party for Jesus | *The rising of Jesus from the dead, celebrated at Easter | A journey across the sea
exercise: «The wheat is a sign of new life and resurrection» in kutia. What does the wheat stand for? | A dry, dusty harvest | Honey and poppy seeds | A Christmas present | *New life and resurrection
exercise: Someone says «the old toy craze has had a resurrection». What does this mean? | The toy craze was broken and thrown away | *The toy craze has come back into use | The toy craze was hidden in a box | The toy craze was sold in a shop
test: «Easter Sunday celebrates the Resurrection.» What is Easter Sunday celebrating? | Jesus being born | *Jesus rising from the dead | The end of winter | A king's birthday
test: Ellie believes that Christians will meet again in the resurrection. What is the resurrection in this sentence? | A type of prayer | A church choir | *A time when the dead are raised to new life | A holiday in the spring
exam: Read «After the resurrection Jesus asked Peter three times, "Do you love me?"». What does after the resurrection mean here? | Before Jesus was born | *Later, after Jesus had risen from the dead | During a storm at sea | After a long holiday
